  "reportPlaceNote": "Report this note",
  "thisPlaceNote": "this note",
  "guideS16L5": "Guestbook: open a place's card while you're inside (within about 40 m) to read what people who sat here before left behind, and leave a line for the next person. Notes are anonymous and disappear after 30 days. You can leave one note per place per day, tap a note to translate it, and report anything that bothers you. When you open the guestbook, your phone sends your location to our server to confirm you're inside; the server doesn't keep it.",
  "quantumWorld": "Quantum World",
  "quantumWorldSubtitle": "One room for the whole world, without revealing where you are",
  "quantumIntroTitle": "Enter the Quantum World",
  "quantumIntroBody": "Everyone in the Quantum World right now shares one room, arranged as a hive around Taipei 101. You get a seat such as \"Q4-17\" — the smaller the ring, the closer to the origin.\n\nNo one can see your real location. Others see only your seat, fixed at the moment you tap Enter; it does not move when you walk. To change it, leave and enter again. Your nickname and mood stay the same, and you can still send glimmers, knock and chat, with tap-to-translate.\n\nWhile you are in the Quantum World you temporarily leave the normal radar and Parallel Universe; when you leave, you return to your check-in spot.",
