  "guideS17Title": "13. Quantum World",
  "guideS17L1": "Tap the hive icon at the top right of the radar (below Parallel Universe), read the note and tap Enter. You enter by tapping each time, just like checking in; every time you open the app you start on the normal radar.",
  "guideS17L2": "Everyone in the Quantum World shares one room: a hive around Taipei 101, with seats 100 m apart. You get a seat code such as \"Q4-17\" (ring 4, seat 17) — smaller rings are closer to the origin. New arrivals fill seats others have left first; rings 1–3 are reserved for gathering hosts.",
  "guideS17L3": "No one can see your real location: others see only your seat. Each time you tap Enter counts as a check-in, and your seat stays fixed from that moment; it does not move when you walk. To change it, leave and enter again. The Quantum World is not available in mainland China.",
  "guideS17L4": "Your nickname and mood stay the same, and you can still send glimmers, knock and chat, with tap-to-translate. Pinch out to see the whole hive; far-away people become points of light. Tap your seat code at the top left to see who's online, turn on Quantum Quiet (no knocks, glimmers still arrive), or leave.",
  "guideS17L5": "There are no whispers, letters to the future, Mood Places, City Beacon or gatherings in the Quantum World. While inside you temporarily leave the normal radar and Parallel Universe; when you leave, your bubble dissolves into light and you return to your check-in spot. If the app is closed or offline for more than 3 minutes, your seat is released.",
